<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>Monica Daily Growth Brief — 22 July 2026</title></head><body style="margin:0;background:#f3f6f8;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#1f2937;line-height:1.45"><div style="max-width:850px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;padding:28px"><div style="border-bottom:5px solid #0f766e;padding-bottom:16px"><div style="font-size:12px;color:#0f766e;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:1px">ALFRED TRAVEL</div><h1 style="margin:5px 0 0;font-size:27px;color:#102a43">Monica Daily Growth Brief</h1><div style="font-size:16px;color:#52606d">User Growth, Activation and Retention</div><div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;color:#52606d">Report date: 22 July 2026 · Prepared at 08:00 AEST</div></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Today’s Growth Decision</h2><div style="background:#fff4e5;border-left:5px solid #d97706;padding:14px 16px"><strong>Do not materially scale acquisition. Maintain controlled acquisition and focus the next seven days on reliability, event measurement and booking attribution.</strong><p style="margin:8px 0 0">The latest available complete Metabase window is 13–19 July 2026 UTC: 346 real itineraries, 306 ACTIVE and 54 hard failures. ACTIVE output is 88.4%, but hard failure is 15.6% and the alfred_plus path is 57.4% hard-fail (54/94), so the &lt;5% reliability gate is not met. A runtime refresh was attempted but authenticated dashboard access was unavailable because no Chromium/CDP session was reachable; therefore this is not presented as a current-period refresh.</p></div>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Evidence Freshness</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Source</th><th>Evidence window / data through</th><th>Freshness</th><th>What it can support</th></tr><tr><td>Metabase live snapshot</td><td>Current refresh unavailable on 22 Jul 2026; no authenticated Chromium/CDP session reachable. Last visible snapshot refreshed 21 Jul, rows through 19 Jul UTC.</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Refresh unavailable</strong></td><td>Prior snapshot confirms presence of activity/failures only; not a current complete funnel.</td></tr><tr><td>Metabase latest complete window</td><td>13–19 Jul 2026 UTC; data through 19 Jul</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Historical baseline; not refreshed today</strong></td><td>Real demand, ACTIVE output, hard-failure and mode concentration.</td></tr><tr><td>Firebase / Jessica event analysis</td><td>Current refresh unavailable on 22 Jul; Events explorer was not hydrated/readable because the authenticated browser session was unavailable. No current event window is used.</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Unavailable</strong></td><td>No current activation, Day-1 retention, platform or push decisioning. DAU/old event data cannot substitute.</td></tr><tr><td>GA4</td><td>Last available 7-day view: 12–18 Jul 2026; data through 18 Jul. Current refresh unavailable on 22 Jul.</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Historical pre-launch baseline</strong></td><td>Pre-Website-V2 acquisition and engagement only; no current conversion claim.</td></tr><tr><td>Website and SEO</td><td>Website V2 uploaded/launched 20 Jul 2026; repo and public assets validated through 20 Jul. First 24–72h remains observation period.</td><td style="color:#b45309"><strong>Early post-launch observation</strong></td><td>Publish status, indexation surfaces and CTA paths; not V2 lift.</td></tr><tr><td>Social / creative intelligence</td><td>Helen tools-status check 22 Jul 2026; current browser batch blocked by CDP connection refusal. No verified fresh creative ranking.</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Access blocked</strong></td><td>Cannot support current creative scaling or post-level claims.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Growth Scorecard</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Area</th><th>Latest validated result</th><th>Assessment</th><th>Next gate</th></tr><tr><td>Real itinerary demand</td><td>346, 13–19 Jul UTC; [SAMPLE] and internal/test rows excluded</td><td>Demand exists, but evidence is not refreshed today.</td><td>Fresh 7-day extract with user/source joins.</td></tr><tr><td>ACTIVE output</td><td>306/346 = <strong>88.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Above 85% broad gate.</td><td>Hold until mode-level failures are repaired.</td></tr><tr><td>Overall hard-failure rate</td><td>54/346 = <strong>15.6%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c"><strong>Reliability blocked.</strong></td><td>&lt;5% on a fresh complete window.</td></tr><tr><td>Primary-mode hard-failure rate</td><td>alfred_plus: 54/94 = <strong>57.4%</strong>, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td style="color:#b91c1c">Critical path failing.</td><td>&lt;5% with reasons reconciled.</td></tr><tr><td>Cleanest-performing mode</td><td>Rows without a normalized mode flag: 306 ACTIVE, 0 hard failures / 346, 13–19 Jul UTC</td><td>Promising but taxonomy is incomplete; not a causal comparison.</td><td>Normalize generation-mode coverage.</td></tr><tr><td>Day-1 retention</td><td>Current Firebase event-level result unavailable</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Hydrated overall cohort result.</td></tr><tr><td>Android retention</td><td>Current Firebase result unavailable</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>Android D1 cohort and event path.</td></tr><tr><td>iOS retention</td><td>Current Firebase result unavailable</td><td>Measurement blocked.</td><td>iOS D1 cohort and event path.</td></tr><tr><td>Push-notification performance</td><td>Current event/campaign refresh unavailable</td><td>Do not infer from DAU.</td><td>FCM coverage, delivered/opened and return session.</td></tr><tr><td>Trustworthy bookings</td><td>No current validated unique-confirmation reconciliation</td><td>Not a scaling signal.</td><td>One confirmation ID mapped to one user journey.</td></tr><tr><td>Sample-data pollution</td><td>[SAMPLE] and internal/test rows excluded from the 346 production KPI</td><td>Production KPI treatment is correct for the available extract.</td><td>Repeat exclusion in fresh pull.</td></tr><tr><td>Organic acquisition</td><td>GA4 baseline: 42 google/organic active users and 63 organic-search sessions, 12–18 Jul; pre-launch</td><td>Useful baseline, not V2 impact.</td><td>Fresh post-launch users and sessions separately.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">What is Working</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Signal</th><th>Evidence</th><th>How Monica should use it</th></tr><tr><td>Real demand exists</td><td>346 real itineraries, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Protect demand with a reliable path before adding paid volume.</td></tr><tr><td>Broad output clears the gate</td><td>306 ACTIVE / 346 = 88.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Use as a recovery target, not scale permission.</td></tr><tr><td>Failure is concentrated</td><td>54/94 alfred_plus hard failures = 57.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Prioritize the failing path rather than broad undirected changes.</td></tr><tr><td>Organic is a meaningful pre-launch surface</td><td>GA4 12–18 Jul: 42 google/organic active users; 63 organic-search sessions.</td><td>Use Website V2 to capture intent, then measure downstream activation.</td></tr><tr><td>V2 has clear conversion surfaces</td><td>Repo through 20 Jul includes Plan a trip CTA, itinerary examples, app links and analytics.js.</td><td>Observe instrumentation/indexing for 72h before claiming lift.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Largest Growth Leaks</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Leak</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Business impact</th></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>alfred_plus generation reliability</td><td>54 hard failures / 94 real = 57.4%, 13–19 Jul UTC.</td><td>Users fail before activation; paid traffic amplifies waste.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Overall reliability above scale gate</td><td>54 / 346 = 15.6%, 13–19 Jul UTC vs &lt;5% gate.</td><td>Planner trust and repeat use are at risk.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Current retention/event observability</td><td>Firebase Events explorer not hydrated/readable on 22 Jul; no current event window.</td><td>Cannot diagnose activation, Android/iOS retention or push impact.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Booking attribution</td><td>No current unique-confirmation reconciliation available.</td><td>Monetization and payback cannot guide acquisition.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Cross-system acquisition reconciliation</td><td>GA4 12–18 Jul is a web/session view; Metabase 13–19 Jul is itinerary grain; no current user-level join.</td><td>Channel quality cannot be assigned confidently.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Creative intelligence access</td><td>Helen’s 22 Jul browser batch blocked by CDP connection refusal.</td><td>Creative choices would rely on unverified evidence.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Seven-Day Action Plan</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Priority</th><th>Action</th><th>Owner</th><th>Success measure</th><th>Scaling gate</th></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Triage alfred_plus by route, provider, timeout and response reason; add safe fallback.</td><td>Engineering</td><td>alfred_plus hard-failure &lt;5% over a fresh 7-day complete window.</td><td>Keep acquisition controlled until met.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Restore authenticated dashboard access and hydrate Firebase Events; publish canonical funnel table.</td><td>Jessica / Analytics</td><td>Fresh signup → first_open → generate → ACTIVE → view/save/share → return events, overall/Android/iOS.</td><td>Measurement unblocked only after row-level event validation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P0</strong></td><td>Reconcile booking confirmation IDs to itinerary and user journey; deduplicate writes.</td><td>Data / Engineering</td><td>100% counted bookings have one unique confirmation ID and journey mapping; duplicate rate reported.</td><td>No monetization scaling claim before reconciliation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Join GA4 source/session to signup, first itinerary and downstream intent at user/cohort grain.</td><td>Growth Analytics</td><td>One comparable source-by-platform cohort table with qualified generation and ACTIVE rate.</td><td>Scale only channels with validated downstream activation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P1</strong></td><td>Improve first-week return after successful itinerary and validate notification readiness.</td><td>Product / CRM</td><td>Fresh D1 and 7-day return by Android/iOS plus FCM delivered/opened events.</td><td>Controlled messaging until retention is stable.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P2</strong></td><td>Run one capped Website V2 CTA/landing test after instrumentation stabilizes.</td><td>Jessica / Growth</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation per organic session, with ACTIVE and hard-failure guardrails.</td><td>Stop if reliability or attribution cannot be measured.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Recommended Growth Experiments</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Experiment</th><th>Proposition</th><th>Primary success metric</th><th>Secondary metrics</th></tr><tr><td>Reliable-path CTA test</td><td>Route qualified web visitors to the validated itinerary path.</td><td>Qualified generation → successful ACTIVE itinerary rate.</td><td>CTA click, webapp arrival, hard failures, time to ACTIVE.</td></tr><tr><td>First-plan return prompt</td><td>After ACTIVE, prompt one practical next action: view, save or share.</td><td>Return session within 7 days.</td><td>Itinerary view, save/share, D1 retention by platform.</td></tr><tr><td>Intent-led V2 landing test</td><td>Compare family/multi-city logistics copy with generic AI-planning copy after GA4 wiring is validated.</td><td>Qualified itinerary generation per organic session.</td><td>CTA click, engagement, ACTIVE output, booking intent.</td></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Billy’s Decisions Today</h2><table cellpadding="7" cellspacing="0" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px"><tr style="background:#0f766e;color:#fff"><th>Decision required</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr><tr><td>Acquisition budget</td><td>Approve controlled acquisition only; no material paid scaling until hard failure is &lt;5% on a fresh complete window and Firebase/booking attribution are trustworthy.</td></tr><tr><td>P0 ownership</td><td>Assign Engineering, Jessica/Analytics and Data/Engineering owners for alfred_plus, Firebase hydration and booking reconciliation this week.</td></tr><tr><td>Website V2 readout</td><td>Approve a 72-hour instrumentation/indexing observation period, followed by a 7-day post-launch baseline; do not call pre-launch GA4 a V2 lift.</td></tr></table>
<h2 style="color:#0f766e;font-size:20px;margin:24px 0 8px">Overall Status</h2><p style="font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;color:#b91c1c;border-top:3px solid #b91c1c;padding-top:12px">Growth status: Reliability blocked</p><p>Available Metabase evidence shows demand but fails the reliability gate, while current Firebase, GA4 and social refreshes were unavailable in the runtime session. The next decision should be measurement and reliability recovery, not material acquisition scaling.</p><p style="font-size:11px;color:#667085;border-top:1px solid #d0d5dd;padding-top:10px">Evidence note: percentages independently recalculated from the latest available Metabase extract; [SAMPLE] and internal/test rows excluded. Current refresh unavailable is explicitly disclosed for Metabase, Firebase, GA4 and social; no stale window is presented as current.</p></div></body></html>
